    {
      "question": "e-11025",
      "field": null,
      "attribute": "question/worked-solution",
      "old_sha256": "87b8782173df2974c8ea6f95349d15279bea28bb74293eb284671ad88a74b21f",
      "new_sha256": "d6cd3ef0921c103ca3e5a375bc95e1036c3e20b4eb8dfc9c13cb0bf1ff73481a",
      "category": "ma_capture",
      "authoring": [],
      "source": [
        {
          "question": "e-11025",
          "field": null,
          "attribute": "question/worked-solution",
          "value": "To evaluate our multivariable function at the point $(10,3),$ we substitute $x = 10$ and $y = 3$ into the function expression:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(10,3) & =({y}^{2}-{log}_{3}\u2061(x-7)){|}_{(10,3)} \\\\  & ={3}^{2}-{log}_{3}\u2061(10-7) \\\\  & =9-{log}_{3}\u2061(3) \\\\  & =9-1 \\\\  & =8.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $f(10,3)=8.$",
          "category": "ma_capture",
          "file": "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041908/example-11025.json",
          "file_sha256": "0823c6262f2b1f30e50451ec1d4284040ccfff8d28e80e74f65e69db7446acf3"
        }
